---
source: crates/pse-host/src/cli.rs
expression: "format!(\"-h\\n{short}\\n--help\\n{long}\")"
---
-h
Read exact artifact ranges with native validators; this does not decode a protocol

Usage: pse inspect artifact [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>

Options:
  -C <checkout>
      --offset <OFFSET>      [default: 0]
      --format <FORMAT>      Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations [env: PSE_FORMAT] [default: auto] [possible values: auto, human, json, ndjson]
      --length <LENGTH>
      --all
      --fields <FIELDS>      Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage
      --budget <BUDGET>      Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts
      --if-match <IF_MATCH>
  -h, --help                 Print help (see more with '--help')
--help
Read exact artifact ranges with native validators; this does not decode a protocol

Usage: pse inspect artifact [OPTIONS] <FILE>

Arguments:
  <FILE>


Options:
  -C <checkout>


      --offset <OFFSET>
          [default: 0]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Human output on terminals, JSON on pipes, or compact NDJSON observations

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Human for a terminal, JSON for pipes
          - human:  Concise summary and pretty structured detail
          - json:   One JSON envelope
          - ndjson: Compact normalized records followed by an observation summary

          [env: PSE_FORMAT]
          [default: auto]

      --length <LENGTH>


      --all


      --fields <FIELDS>
          Select comma-separated payload fields while retaining identity, state and coverage

      --budget <BUDGET>
          Limit whole payload records; producer pages retain their omission and continuation facts

      --if-match <IF_MATCH>


  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
